==Trivia==
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s name derives from the Finnish name for "''Peter''", which in turn comes from the Greek name "''Petros''", meaning stone.
*The acronym for P.E.K.K.A. didn't officially stand for anything in particular originally. Supercell held a Facebook contest on 22 August 2012 to see who could come up with the best written-out name for P.E.K.K.A as judged by the number of likes the comment received. The name "''Perfectly Enraged Knight Killer of Assassins''" was the winner. The person who submitted the acronym was called Víctor in the [https://www.facebook.com/ClashofClans/photos/478339952190333 Facebook announcement].
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], and [[Balloon]].
*He is 1 of 3 troops that are “miniature” versions of another troop in Clash of Clans, the others being the Baby Dragon and [[Electro Dragon]]. They are a smaller version of [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/P.E.K.K.A P.E.K.K.A.], [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Dragon Dragon], and [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Electro_Dragon Electro Dragon], respectively.
**In the Arabic, Thai, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s name translates to "Small P.E.K.K.A.", "Tiny P.E.K.K.A.", and "Little P.E.K.K.A." respectively.
**According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=BRING-YOUR-CHILD-TO-WORK-DAY_Final.jpg strip], the Mini P.E.K.K.A. is the P.E.K.K.A.'s child.
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is 1 of 10 troops that have been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Special Delivery|Special Delivery]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the others being Knight, [[Skeleton Barrel]], Musketeer, Wizard, P.E.K.K.A., [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Golem]], [[Sparky]], and [[Royal Ghost]].
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is 1 of 3 troops that have had its Melee range classification changed, the others being Giant and P.E.K.K.A..
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s gender has been confirmed as male, as the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UfNcIMpLv5o Mini P.E.K.K.A. commercial] referred to Mini P.E.K.K.A. as "he" and "him", despite being based on a female troop, the P.E.K.K.A..
**The Clash of Clans Facebook account erroneously referred to the Mini P.E.K.K.A. as a she in a [https://www.facebook.com/ClashofClans/posts/pfbid02rKk27v67K9HuBFzFdmUbMrHdMEQ8nETBq4HPtnSD7iu5W15ZoB1WptnuYFR8br8tl?__cft__&#x5B;0&#x5D;=AZVoj9lkS5pqSSI48FD8Xzl1DsFiFfv_fvSBUAOashs1PB7Cdac78sGCEv9ZeYs9maKA_qzOJmz6iTFrb9T920AnST1CH2fKjYefb2FjDE2SoZndBGEXJSf_IHlFcvVEzd7TpQYU0bTQxTjvwcDBXK2ZAdIiY8J8oZRRSN0P6jWwSeiPSKapD54pDFMMGxRnIZ8HsCK8IKYWOZTV3TUD4S4-&__tn__=%2CO%2CP-y-R post].
*His description is a reference to the Clash of Clans [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nmlIkSvezkU P.E.K.K.A. commercial].
**Even though his description states that the [[Arenas|Arena]] is a butterfly-free zone, a butterfly can be seen flying in the Training Camp picture, and butterflies fly in Rascal's Hideout.
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A., along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A., Giant Skeleton, Golem, [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Skeleton King]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A., along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Ice Spirit, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, Prince, and [[Night Witch]], is featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Goblins, Skeletons, Barbarians, Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and [[Princess]], he is also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. has a passion towards pancakes. His passion of pancakes is referenced a few times:
**When deployed, the Mini P.E.K.K.A. will say "''Pancakes''".
***If the [[Royal Chef]] throws a pancake to a Mini P.E.K.K.A., the Mini P.E.K.K.A. will say "''Pancakes''" in a higher pitched voiced than his normal deploy sound.
***The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Mega Minion, Wizard, Hog Rider, P.E.K.K.A., [[Dark Prince]], Bowler, [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], Princess, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
**A [https://twitter.com/ClashRoyale/status/759055983381360640?s=20&t=5xU2JkgTzrZ2n-3aaPRolA tweet] by the Clash Royale official Twitter account which had a real life Mini P.E.K.K.A standing next to a Giant Skeleton, with the caption "Who wants pancakes?".
**[https://youtu.be/dIXbEtVWBMo The trailer for the Crown Duel tournament] shows a man eating pancakes while the Mini P.E.K.K.A's deploy sound plays.
**In [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9I9WOg0DwE0 an Emote trailer] depicting him for his [[Emotes]].
**The PANCAKES! Arena that was featured during [[Pass Royale|Season 37]], Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s Dream.
**The Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s card render depicts a pancake on Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s head.
**The [https://clashroyale.fandom.com/wiki/Battle_Banners?file=Pancaked_Decoration.png Pancaked Decoration] saying "''It's rude to throw a pancake at somebody. Unless that somebody is Mini P.E.K.K.A!''".
**His description in Merge Tactics which says "''A lightly armored heavy hitter with a soft spot for pancakes''".
**His Hero form, its card image, and its ability ability depicts pancakes. Its description also says "''Hero Mini P.E.K.K.A has finally perfected his pancake recipe by speeding up cooking time with each attack! Stacks on stacks on stacks!''" and its ability's decription says "''Eats pancakes to level up. The longer you wait, the more pancakes he cooks!''".
*The [[Furnace]]'s description could be a reference towards the Mini P.E.K.K.A. since the Mini P.E.K.K.A. says "''Pancakes''" when he is deployed in the Arena.
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is one of the first cards that the player unlocks, as a reward for the player winning the first Tutorial match through a Wooden [[Chests|Chest]], alongside the Musketeer.
**Unlike the Musketeer, the player is told to use the Mini P.E.K.K.A. during the tutorial.
*The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is the subject of a few Emotes.
**The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Mini P.E.K.K.A. is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the Dart Goblin, P.E.K.K.A., Prince, Giant Skeleton, Mega Knight, [[Super Witch]], and the Golden Knight.
***The Night of the Living P.E.K.K.A. frame is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_of_the_Living_Dead Night of the Living Dead]. Its description says "''They're coming to get you, Barbarian!''", which is also a reference to the same film.
*In the [https://youtu.be/zWW1dtcsDGk?si=Ytadsvv1hpz23v9y Card Mastery intro video], the Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s Damage Dealer [[Card Mastery]] task was shown to require the Mini P.E.K.K.A. to deal 151,000 damage. However, it was lowered to 150,000 in-game.
*Before the Mini P.E.K.K.A.'s card release, the Mini P.E.K.K.A. was supposed to be an {{Rarity|Epic}} card. However, he was changed to a {{Rarity|Rare}} card post-release.

